# Derived packaging artifacts — rebuilt from tracked sources
HIVOLT-deliverables.zip
HIVOLT-image-fix.zip

# Staged copies of files already tracked at their source paths.
# Only the folder's README is tracked, since it is the index and exists nowhere else.
HIVOLT-deliverables/docs/
HIVOLT-deliverables/model/
HIVOLT-deliverables/theme-snippets/
HIVOLT-storefront.zip

# Ruflo local secrets and runtime data
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.claude-flow/data/
.claude-flow/logs/
.claude-flow/sessions/
.claude-flow/metrics/
.claude-flow/security/
.swarm/
# A gitignore pattern containing a slash is anchored to this file's directory,
# so the five above only ever matched .claude-flow/ at the repo root. Ruflo
# writes its state next to whatever directory a command runs in -- a Bash call
# with cwd site/theme/ left site/theme/.claude-flow/ untracked. These are
# session and policy state for the tooling, not store work, so they are ignored
# wherever they land rather than committed.
**/.claude-flow/
**/.swarm/
ruvector.db
ruvector.db-journal

# Generated by site/build-theme.py from tracked sources
build/
HIVOLT-theme.zip

# Downscaled copies of the tracked site/shot-*.png screenshots, made only to
# get under the file-delivery size limit. Regenerate with Pillow when needed.
site/sm-shot-*.jpg
.claude-flow/daemon-state.json
.claude-flow/harness-active-policy.json
.claude-flow/policy/
.claude/proven-config.json
.claude/.proven-config-version
.claude-flow/daemon.pid
*.pid

# video-shotcraft ships a 36MB / 154-file MP3 sound-design library. The skill
# itself (shot cards, references, template, demos, components) is tracked; the
# audio is not, because git keeps binary blobs in history permanently and this
# would roughly quintuple the repo. Re-fetch when sound design is needed:
#   git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/Vincentwei1021/video-shotcraft.git
#   cp -r video-shotcraft/assets/audio .claude/skills/video-shotcraft/assets/
.claude/skills/video-shotcraft/assets/audio/

# Python bytecode. Build artefacts, never source — two of these were committed
# by accident earlier (audit/__pycache__) and are untracked in the same commit
# that adds this rule.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
qa/node_modules/
